IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rp-dates`

-- Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932 (Tas), Part VII (representative proceedings, ss 64-89D, inserted by No. 14 of
-- 2019 from 9 September 2019) -- the rules a person with a claim meets when they bring a representative proceeding (a
-- class action) in the Supreme Court of Tasmania or are a group member in one: when the Part applies (ss 64, 65), who may
-- start one (ss 66, 67), who is a group member (ss 68, 69), opting out (s 71), joining later (s 72), the Court stopping
-- the proceeding as a class action and what follows (ss 73-76), costs (ss 78, 89A), replacing the representative party
-- (ss 80, 83(3)), stay of execution (s 81), settlement (ss 82, 83), notices (ss 84, 85(8)), aggregate damages (s 86(3)),
-- claiming from a fund (s 87), the effect of the judgment (s 88), a group member's appeal when the representative party
-- does not appeal (s 89(3)), suspension of limitation periods (s 89B) and reimbursement of the representative party's
-- costs (s 89D).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in rp-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule. Nothing
-- here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, an "if"
-- or "unless" condition that fails, "may not", "must not", "is not to ... unless", "other than", a period the text
-- fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Court's
-- judgments ("satisfied", "appears to the Court", "thinks fit", "just") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them,
-- never a guess at them. Forks (Fn) are listed in NOTES.md.
--
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (CC BY 4.0, State of Tasmania). For the
-- latest information on Tasmanian Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au. Unofficial copy; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part VII -- representative proceedings: the rules`

§§ `Division 1 -- when the Part applies (ss 64, 65)`

-- s 65: "This Part applies to proceedings commenced after the commencement of this section, whether the cause of action
-- arose before, or arises after, that commencement." Section 65 was inserted by No. 14 of 2019, s 10, "Applied:09 Sep
-- 2019". A proceeding commenced on 9 September 2019 itself is taken as commenced after the commencement (fork F1).
`s 65 -- the day Part VII commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 9 9 2019

DECLARE `Kind of proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania`
    `a criminal proceeding`
    `a proceeding in another court`

-- s 64: "proceedings means proceedings in the Court, other than criminal proceedings". A "means" definition: a criminal
-- proceeding, or a proceeding in another court, is not a proceeding for the Part (JUST FALSE). A proceeding commenced
-- before 9 September 2019 is outside s 65's scope, which has no "only": NOTHING. The cause of action may be older.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of proceeding`, `the day it was commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 64, 65 -- Part VII applies to the proceeding` `the kind` `the day it was commenced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a criminal proceeding` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a proceeding in another court` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a civil proceeding in the Supreme Court of Tasmania` THEN
        IF `the days from` `s 65 -- the day Part VII commenced` `to` `the day it was commenced` AT LEAST 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": s 65 says what the Part applies to; the Part as repealed in 2001 is not encoded)

§§ `Division 2 -- starting a representative proceeding (ss 66, 67)`

-- s 66(1): "Subject to this Part, if - (a) 7 or more persons have claims against the same person; and (b) the claims of all
-- those persons are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances; and (c) the claims of all
-- those persons give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact - proceedings may be commenced by one or more of
-- those persons as representing some or all of them." s 67(1): "a person has a sufficient interest to commence
-- representative proceedings against another person on behalf of other persons if the person has standing to commence
-- proceedings on the person's own behalf against that other person." s 66(2): the kind of relief (equitable relief,
-- damages, damages needing individual assessment, different relief for each person) and separate contracts or acts do not
-- matter, so they are not asked. "if" conditions, and "by one or more of those persons": when a limb fails, JUST FALSE.
-- The count includes the person asking (fork F2).
GIVEN `Part VII applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `how many persons have claims against the same defendant` IS A NUMBER
      `I have a claim against that defendant myself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 66(1), 67(1) -- I may commence a representative proceeding` `Part VII applies` `how many persons have claims against the same defendant` `I have a claim against that defendant myself` `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances` `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact` MEANS
    IF `Part VII applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF     `how many persons have claims against the same defendant` AT LEAST 7
            AND `I have a claim against that defendant myself`
            AND `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances`
            AND `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE `Part VII applies`

-- s 67(3): "If a person has commenced representative proceedings, that person retains standing - (a) to continue the
-- proceedings; and (b) to bring an appeal from a judgment in the proceedings - even though the person ceases to have a
-- claim against any defendant." For a person who did not commence the proceeding the subsection says nothing: NOTHING.
GIVEN `I commenced the representative proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(3) -- I keep standing to continue and to appeal` `I commenced the representative proceeding` MEANS
    IF `I commenced the representative proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 67(3) speaks only of the person who commenced the proceeding)

§§ `Division 2 -- who is a group member (ss 64, 68, 69, 70)`

DECLARE `Who I am, for s 68` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, a company or another private body`
    `an officer of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, acting in that capacity`
    `a Minister of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
    `the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
    `a body corporate established by law for a public purpose (not an incorporated company or association)`

-- s 64: "group member means a member of a group of persons on whose behalf representative proceedings have been
-- commenced"; s 70(1)(a): the originating process must "describe or otherwise identify the group members"; s 70(2): no
-- need to name them or give their number. s 68(1): "the consent of a person to be a group member is not required." (2):
-- "None of the following is a group member in representative proceedings unless the person gives consent in writing to
-- being so: (a) the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (b) a Minister ...; (c) a body corporate established for a public
-- purpose by a law ..., other than an incorporated company or incorporated association; (d) an officer ..., in his or her
-- capacity as an officer." Outside the group description: JUST FALSE (the "means" definition; fork F3). Listed and no
-- written consent: JUST FALSE ("unless").
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am, for s 68`
      `I fall within the group as the originating process describes it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have consented in writing to be a group member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 64, 68 -- I am a group member` `who I am` `I fall within the group as the originating process describes it` `I have consented in writing to be a group member` MEANS
    IF NOT `I fall within the group as the originating process describes it`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `who I am`
         WHEN `an individual, a company or another private body` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE IF `I have consented in writing to be a group member` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Group member under a legal incapacity` IS ONE OF
    `s 69 does not apply: I am not under a legal incapacity`
    `I am a group member without a substitute decision-maker, and this step may be taken by my substitute decision-maker (s 69(2), (3))`
    `I am a group member without a substitute decision-maker, but this step can only be taken by a substitute decision-maker (s 69(3))`

-- s 69(1): "substitute decision-maker means a person who has a legal right or legal obligation to make decisions for
-- another person." (2): "It is not necessary for a person under legal incapacity to have a substitute decision-maker
-- merely in order to be a group member." (3): "A group member who is a person under legal incapacity may only take a step
-- in representative proceedings, or conduct part of the proceedings, by means of the member's substitute decision-maker."
GIVEN `I am under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step is taken by my substitute decision-maker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Group member under a legal incapacity`
`s 69 -- a group member under a legal incapacity` `I am under a legal incapacity` `the step is taken by my substitute decision-maker` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am under a legal incapacity`
    THEN `s 69 does not apply: I am not under a legal incapacity`
    ELSE IF `the step is taken by my substitute decision-maker`
         THEN `I am a group member without a substitute decision-maker, and this step may be taken by my substitute decision-maker (s 69(2), (3))`
         ELSE `I am a group member without a substitute decision-maker, but this step can only be taken by a substitute decision-maker (s 69(3))`

§§ `Division 2 -- opting out (s 71)`

-- s 71(1): "The Court is to fix a date before which a group member may opt out of representative proceedings in the
-- Court." (2): "A group member may opt out of the representative proceedings by written notice given before the date so
-- fixed." (3): the Court may, on application by a group member, the representative party or the defendant, fix another
-- date so as to extend the period. (4): "Except with the leave of the Court, the hearing of representative proceedings
-- must not commence earlier than the date before which a group member may opt out of the proceedings."
--
-- "before the date so fixed": the last day for the notice is the day before the date fixed (or the date as extended).
-- The period is a regulative rule: the group member DOes give written notice WITHIN the days from the day the proceeding
-- was commenced (day 0) to that last day, LEST BREACH. The "breach" is not a wrong: it is the loss of the right to opt
-- out, so that the member stays in the group and is bound by the judgment (s 88), unless the Court fixes a later date
-- under s 71(3).
DECLARE `Opt-out party` IS ONE OF `the group member`
DECLARE `Opt-out act` IS ONE OF `give written notice of opting out`

GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 71(2) -- the last day to give an opt-out notice` `the date fixed for opting out` MEANS `the day before` `the date fixed for opting out`

GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Opt-out party` `Opt-out act`
`s 71(2) -- opt out by written notice before the date fixed` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `the date fixed for opting out` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    DO `give written notice of opting out`
    WITHIN (`the days from` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `to` (`s 71(2) -- the last day to give an opt-out notice` `the date fixed for opting out`))
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "no written notice before the date fixed: the member has not opted out, stays in the group and is bound by the judgment (ss 71(2), 88), unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))"

-- Runs the rule over a notice given at a time. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not
-- BREACH: FULFILLED means in time, anything else late. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Opt-out party` `Opt-out act`
      `the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an opt-out notice is in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time`), (EVENT `the group member` `give written notice of opting out` `the time`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my opting out stands` IS ONE OF
    `opted out: written notice given before the date fixed (s 71(2))`
    `still open: I can opt out by written notice given before the date fixed`
    `too late: I have not opted out, unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))`

-- A notice not in writing is no opt-out (s 71(2) "by written notice"); while the period is open the member may still give
-- a written one. A notice dated before the proceeding was commenced is outside the encoding (it is not tested).
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE
      `I have given a written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where my opting out stands`
`s 71 -- where my opting out stands` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `the date fixed for opting out` `I have given a written notice` `the day I gave it` `today` MEANS
    IF `I have given a written notice`
    THEN IF `an opt-out notice is in time under` `the rule` `at` (`the days from` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `to` `the day I gave it`)
         THEN `opted out: written notice given before the date fixed (s 71(2))`
         ELSE `too late: I have not opted out, unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))`
    ELSE IF `an opt-out notice is in time under` `the rule` `at` (`the days from` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `to` `today`)
         THEN `still open: I can opt out by written notice given before the date fixed`
         ELSE `too late: I have not opted out, unless the Court fixes a later date (s 71(3))`
    WHERE
        `the rule` MEANS `s 71(2) -- opt out by written notice before the date fixed` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `the date fixed for opting out`

-- s 71(4): "must not commence earlier than the date" -- the hearing may begin on the date fixed itself. Earlier: JUST FALSE
-- ("Except with the leave of the Court"), JUST TRUE with leave.
GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE
      `the day the hearing begins` IS A DATE
      `the Court has given leave to begin earlier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(4) -- the hearing may begin on that day` `the date fixed for opting out` `the day the hearing begins` `the Court has given leave to begin earlier` MEANS
    IF `the days from` `the date fixed for opting out` `to` `the day the hearing begins` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the Court has given leave to begin earlier` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 2 -- a claim that arises after the proceeding began (s 72)`

-- s 72(1): on the representative party's application, at any stage, "the Court may give leave to amend the originating
-- process ... so as to alter the description of the group." (2): "The description of the group may be altered so as to
-- include a person - (a) whose cause of action accrued after the commencement of the representative proceedings but before
-- such date as the Court fixes when giving leave under subsection (1); and (b) who would have been included in the group,
-- or with the consent of the person would have been included in the group, if the cause of action had accrued before the
-- commencement of the proceedings." (4): the Court may order notice and an opt-out date for them.
-- A cause of action accruing on the day of commencement is not "after" it (fork F4); one accruing on the date fixed is not
-- "before" it. Outside (2)(a) or (b) the grant does not reach the person: NOTHING (limited by its own wording). With both
-- limbs met, the answer turns on the leave: JUST TRUE with it; without it the group description is not altered, JUST FALSE
-- (fork F5).
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
      `the date the Court fixes when giving leave` IS A DATE
      `I would have been included had it accrued before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court gives leave to amend the group description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72 -- the group may be altered to include me` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `the day my cause of action accrued` `the date the Court fixes when giving leave` `I would have been included had it accrued before the commencement` `the Court gives leave to amend the group description` MEANS
    IF     `the days from` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `to` `the day my cause of action accrued` GREATER THAN 0
       AND `the days from` `the day my cause of action accrued` `to` `the date the Court fixes when giving leave` GREATER THAN 0
       AND `I would have been included had it accrued before the commencement`
    THEN IF `the Court gives leave to amend the group description` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 72(2) reaches only a person whose cause of action accrued in the window and who would otherwise have been in the group)

§§ `Division 2 -- the Court stopping the proceeding as a class action (ss 73-76)`

DECLARE `Section 75 ground` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `(a) the costs as a class action are likely to exceed the costs of separate proceedings`
    `(b) all the relief can be obtained by proceedings other than representative proceedings`
    `(c) it will not be an efficient and effective means of dealing with the claims`
    `(d) the representative party cannot adequately represent the group members`
    `(e) it is otherwise inappropriate to pursue the claims as a class action`
    `only that the group does not include everyone who might have been included, or is aggregated for a purpose such as litigation funding`

-- s 73: "If, at any stage ..., it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members, the Court ... may
-- order that the proceedings continue under this Part or order that the proceedings no longer continue under this Part."
-- s 74: if "(a) the relief claimed ... is or includes payment of money to group members (otherwise than in respect of
-- costs); and (b) on application by the defendant, the Court concludes that it is likely that ... the cost to the
-- defendant of identifying the group members and distributing to them the amounts ... would be excessive ..." the Court
-- may direct that the proceedings no longer continue under the Part (or stay the money relief). s 75(1): "on application
-- by the defendant or of its own motion, may order that representative proceedings no longer continue under this Part if
-- it is satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to do so because" of one of (a)-(e). s 75(2): "it is not
-- inappropriate for claims to be pursued by means of representative proceedings merely because the persons identified as
-- group members ... (a) do not include all persons on whose behalf those proceedings might have been brought; or (b) are
-- aggregated together for a particular purpose such as a litigation funding arrangement." Each route is an "if": when none
-- holds, JUST FALSE under ss 73-75 (s 89C's general power is not read as a further route: fork F6).
GIVEN `it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relief claimed includes payment of money to group members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the defendant's application the Court concludes the cost of identifying members and distributing would be excessive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground` IS A `Section 75 ground`
      `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice because of that ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 73-75 -- the Court may order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action` `it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members` `the relief claimed includes payment of money to group members` `on the defendant's application the Court concludes the cost of identifying members and distributing would be excessive` `the ground` `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice because of that ground` MEANS
    IF    `it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members`
       OR (`the relief claimed includes payment of money to group members` AND `on the defendant's application the Court concludes the cost of identifying members and distributing would be excessive`)
       OR (`a s 75(1) ground` AND `the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice because of that ground`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a s 75(1) ground` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `none` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `only that the group does not include everyone who might have been included, or is aggregated for a purpose such as litigation funding` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `My role` IS ONE OF
    `the representative party`
    `a group member (not the representative party)`

DECLARE `After an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action` IS ONE OF
    `no such order has been made`
    `I may continue the proceeding on my own behalf against the defendant (s 76(1)(a))`
    `I may apply to be joined as a plaintiff, and the Court may order it (s 76(1)(b))`

-- s 76(1): "If the Court makes an order under section 73, 74 or 75 that representative proceedings no longer continue under
-- this Part - (a) the proceedings may be continued as proceedings by the representative party on the party's own behalf
-- against the defendant; and (b) on the application of a person who was a group member ..., the Court may order that the
-- person be joined as an applicant in the proceedings." (2): "applicant ... includes a claimant or plaintiff".
GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role`
      `the Court has ordered under s 73, 74 or 75 that it no longer continue under Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `After an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action`
`s 76 -- what follows an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action` `my role` `the Court has ordered under s 73, 74 or 75 that it no longer continue under Part VII` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court has ordered under s 73, 74 or 75 that it no longer continue under Part VII`
    THEN `no such order has been made`
    ELSE CONSIDER `my role`
         WHEN `the representative party` THEN `I may continue the proceeding on my own behalf against the defendant (s 76(1)(a))`
         WHEN `a group member (not the representative party)` THEN `I may apply to be joined as a plaintiff, and the Court may order it (s 76(1)(b))`

§§ `Division 2 and Division 6 -- costs against a group member (ss 77, 78, 89A)`

DECLARE `The costs in question` IS ONE OF
    `costs of a question that relates only to my claim, where the Court permitted me to appear for it (s 78)`
    `costs connected with a sub-group under s 77`
    `any other costs of the proceeding`

-- s 78(2): "the individual group member, and not the representative party, is liable for costs associated with the
-- determination of the question." s 89A: "the Court may not award costs against a person on whose behalf the proceedings
-- have been commenced (other than a representative party) except as authorised by section 77 or 78." For the
-- representative party Part VII does not shield or speak: NOTHING (the ordinary costs rules, not encoded). s 77 authorises
-- directions and sub-groups but says nothing of costs: NOTHING (finding 3, fork F7).
GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role`
      `the costs` IS A `The costs in question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 78(2), 89A -- costs may be awarded against me` `my role` `the costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `the representative party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 89A excludes the representative party from its protection and says no more)
    WHEN `a group member (not the representative party)` THEN
        CONSIDER `the costs`
        WHEN `costs of a question that relates only to my claim, where the Court permitted me to appear for it (s 78)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `costs connected with a sub-group under s 77` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points to s 77, which is silent on costs; fork F7)
        WHEN `any other costs of the proceeding` THEN JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 2 -- replacing the representative party (ss 80, 83(3))`

DECLARE `Whom I want replaced` IS ONE OF
    `the representative party`
    `the sub-group representative party`

-- s 80(1): "If, on application by a group member, it appears to the Court that a representative party is not able to
-- represent the interests of the group members adequately, the Court may substitute another group member as representative
-- party". (2): the same for a sub-group representative party "on application by a sub-group member". s 83(3): "If a person
-- has sought leave to withdraw as representative party under subsection (2), the Court, on application by a group member,
-- may make an order for the substitution of another group member as representative party". "if": JUST FALSE when no
-- route holds. The person asking is a group member.
GIVEN `whom` IS A `Whom I want replaced`
      `I am a member of that sub-group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court that they cannot represent the members adequately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representative party has sought leave to withdraw under s 83(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 80, 83(3) -- the Court may substitute another on my application` `whom` `I am a member of that sub-group` `it appears to the Court that they cannot represent the members adequately` `the representative party has sought leave to withdraw under s 83(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whom`
    WHEN `the representative party` THEN
        IF `it appears to the Court that they cannot represent the members adequately` OR `the representative party has sought leave to withdraw under s 83(2)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the sub-group representative party` THEN
        IF `I am a member of that sub-group` AND `it appears to the Court that they cannot represent the members adequately`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 2 -- stay of execution (s 81)`

-- s 81: "If a defendant in representative proceedings commences proceedings in the Court against a group member, the Court
-- may order a stay of execution in respect of any relief awarded to the group member in the representative proceedings
-- until the other proceedings are determined." "if": JUST FALSE where the defendant has not sued the member in the Court;
-- "until": JUST FALSE once the other proceedings are determined.
GIVEN `the defendant has commenced proceedings in the Supreme Court against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those other proceedings have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 -- the Court may stay execution of my award` `the defendant has commenced proceedings in the Supreme Court against me` `those other proceedings have been determined` MEANS
    IF `the defendant has commenced proceedings in the Supreme Court against me` AND NOT `those other proceedings have been determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 2 -- settlement and discontinuance (ss 82, 83)`

-- s 82(1): "Representative proceedings may not be settled or discontinued without the approval of the Court." A flat "may
-- not ... without": JUST FALSE without approval. With it, JUST TRUE.
GIVEN `the Court has approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(1) -- the class action may be settled or discontinued` `the Court has approved it` MEANS
    IF `the Court has approved it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 82(3): "Unless the Court is satisfied that it is just to do so, an application for approval of a settlement of
-- representative proceedings may not be determined unless notice has been given to group members in accordance with
-- section 84." JUST FALSE when neither holds.
GIVEN `notice of the application has been given to group members under s 84` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide without that notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(3) -- the settlement approval application may be decided` `notice of the application has been given to group members under s 84` `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide without that notice` MEANS
    IF `notice of the application has been given to group members under s 84` OR `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide without that notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `What I want to do as representative party` IS ONE OF
    `settle my own claim`
    `withdraw as representative party`

-- s 83(1): "A representative party, with the leave of the Court, may settle the party's individual claim in whole or in part
-- at any stage". (2): "If ... the representative party is seeking leave of the Court to settle, or has settled, his or her
-- individual claim, the representative party, with the leave of the Court, may withdraw as representative party." (4):
-- "Before granting ... leave to withdraw - (a) the Court must be satisfied that notice of the application has been given to
-- group members in accordance with section 84(1) and has been given in sufficient time for them to apply to have another
-- person substituted ...; and (b) any application for the substitution of another group member as representative party
-- must have been determined." Without leave the grants do not reach the case: NOTHING (fork F8). (4) is a precondition: if
-- either limb fails, JUST FALSE. Withdrawing when not settling one's own claim: outside (2), NOTHING.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to do as representative party`
      `I am seeking leave to settle, or have settled, my own claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of my withdrawal application was given to group members in time for them to seek a substitute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every application to substitute another representative party has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83 -- I may do this as representative party` `what` `I am seeking leave to settle, or have settled, my own claim` `notice of my withdrawal application was given to group members in time for them to seek a substitute` `every application to substitute another representative party has been determined` `the Court gives leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `settle my own claim` THEN
        IF `the Court gives leave` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 83(1) grants settlement "with the leave of the Court"; fork F8)
    WHEN `withdraw as representative party` THEN
        IF NOT `I am seeking leave to settle, or have settled, my own claim`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 83(2) speaks only of a representative party settling their own claim)
        ELSE IF NOT (`notice of my withdrawal application was given to group members in time for them to seek a substitute` AND `every application to substitute another representative party has been determined`)
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE IF `the Court gives leave` THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "with the leave of the Court"; fork F8)

§§ `Division 3 -- notices (ss 84, 85(8))`

DECLARE `The matter` IS ONE OF
    `the start of the proceeding and my right to opt out before the date fixed`
    `the defendant's application to dismiss the proceeding for want of prosecution`
    `an application to approve a settlement`
    `the representative party's application for leave to withdraw`
    `money paid into Court in answer to a cause of action in the proceeding`
    `some other matter`

-- s 84(1): "Notice must be given to group members of the following matters ...: (a) the commencement of the proceedings and
-- the right of the group members to opt out ...; (b) an application by the defendant ... for the dismissal of the
-- proceedings on the ground of want of prosecution; (c) an application for approval of a settlement; (d) an application by
-- a representative party seeking leave to withdraw ..." (2): "The Court may dispense with compliance with any or all of the
-- requirements of subsection (1) if the relief sought ... does not include any claim for damages." (3): "If the Court so
-- orders, notice must be given to group members of the paying into Court of money in answer to a cause of action ..." (4):
-- "The Court, at any stage, may order that notice of any matter be given to a group member or group members." (5): "as
-- soon as practicable after the occurrence of the event". A dispensation where damages are claimed is not one s 84(2)
-- allows, so the duty stands (fork F10). (3) unordered: "if" fails, JUST FALSE. (4) unordered: silent, NOTHING.
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `The matter`
      `the relief sought includes a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has dispensed with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered notice of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84 -- notice of the matter must be given to group members` `the matter` `the relief sought includes a claim for damages` `the Court has dispensed with the notice` `the Court has ordered notice of it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `money paid into Court in answer to a cause of action in the proceeding` THEN
        IF `the Court has ordered notice of it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `some other matter` THEN
        IF `the Court has ordered notice of it` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 84(4) is a power to order notice of any matter; without an order the Act does not say)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court has dispensed with the notice` AND NOT `the relief sought includes a claim for damages`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 85(8): "The failure of a group member to receive, or respond to, a notice does not affect a step taken, or an order made
-- or judgment given, in any proceedings." A flat "does not": JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `I did not receive, or did not respond to, a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(8) -- my not receiving or answering a notice undoes a step, order or judgment` `I did not receive, or did not respond to, a notice` MEANS
    IF `I did not receive, or did not respond to, a notice`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 85(8) speaks only of a notice not received or not answered)

§§ `Division 4 -- judgment, damages and the fund (ss 86, 87, 88)`

-- s 86(1)(f): "make an award of damages in an aggregate amount without specifying amounts awarded in respect of individual
-- group members." (3): "Subject to section 82, the Court is not to make an award of damages under subsection (1)(f) unless
-- a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount to which group members will be entitled under the
-- judgment." "is not to ... unless": JUST FALSE. "Subject to section 82" is read as lifting the bar where the award gives
-- effect to a settlement the Court approves (fork F11).
GIVEN `the award gives effect to a settlement approved under s 82` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total the group members will be entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(3) -- the Court may award aggregate damages` `the award gives effect to a settlement approved under s 82` `a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total the group members will be entitled to` MEANS
    IF `the award gives effect to a settlement approved under s 82` OR `a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total the group members will be entitled to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 87(3)(c): the order constituting a fund is to "specify a day (which is not earlier than 6 months after the day on which
-- the order is made) on or before which the group members are to make a claim for payment out of the fund". The earliest
-- day the Court may specify: the day 6 calendar months after the order (fork F9).
GIVEN `the day the fund order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 87(3)(c) -- the earliest claim day the Court may specify` `the day the fund order is made` MEANS `the day` 6 `months after` `the day the fund order is made`

-- The claim on the fund is a regulative rule: the group member DOes make a claim WITHIN the days from the order (day 0) to
-- the claim day, "on or before" it, LEST BREACH. The breach is the loss of the right to claim without the Court's
-- allowance. s 87(4): "The Court may allow a group member to make a claim after the day specified under subsection (3)(c)
-- if - (a) the fund has not already been fully distributed or applied in accordance with an order under subsection (5);
-- and (b) it is just to do so."
DECLARE `Fund party` IS ONE OF `the claiming group member`
DECLARE `Fund act` IS ONE OF `make a claim for payment out of the fund`

GIVEN `the day the fund order is made` IS A DATE
      `the claim day specified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Fund party` `Fund act`
`s 87(3)(c) -- claim on the fund on or before the claim day` `the day the fund order is made` `the claim day specified` MEANS
    PARTY `the claiming group member`
    DO `make a claim for payment out of the fund`
    WITHIN (`the days from` `the day the fund order is made` `to` `the claim day specified`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claiming group member` BECAUSE "no claim on or before the day specified: a late claim only if the Court allows it, the fund is not fully distributed and it is just (s 87(4))"

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Fund party` `Fund act`
      `the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fund claim is in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time`), (EVENT `the claiming group member` `make a claim for payment out of the fund` `the time`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my claim on the fund stands` IS ONE OF
    `made in time: on or before the claim day (s 87(3)(c))`
    `still open: I can claim on or before the claim day`
    `late, but the Court may allow it if it is just (s 87(4))`
    `late, and the Court has allowed it (s 87(4))`
    `late, and the Court cannot allow it: the fund has been fully distributed or applied (s 87(4)(a))`

GIVEN `the day the fund order is made` IS A DATE
      `the claim day specified` IS A DATE
      `I have claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I claimed` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the fund has been fully distributed or applied under s 87(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has allowed my late claim as just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where my claim on the fund stands`
`s 87(3)(c), (4) -- where my claim on the fund stands` `the day the fund order is made` `the claim day specified` `I have claimed` `the day I claimed` `today` `the fund has been fully distributed or applied under s 87(5)` `the Court has allowed my late claim as just` MEANS
    IF `a fund claim is in time under` (`s 87(3)(c) -- claim on the fund on or before the claim day` `the day the fund order is made` `the claim day specified`) `at` `the time`
    THEN IF `I have claimed` THEN `made in time: on or before the claim day (s 87(3)(c))` ELSE `still open: I can claim on or before the claim day`
    ELSE BRANCH IF `the fund has been fully distributed or applied under s 87(5)` THEN `late, and the Court cannot allow it: the fund has been fully distributed or applied (s 87(4)(a))`
                IF `the Court has allowed my late claim as just` THEN `late, and the Court has allowed it (s 87(4))`
                OTHERWISE `late, but the Court may allow it if it is just (s 87(4))`
    WHERE
        `the time` MEANS
            IF `I have claimed`
            THEN `the days from` `the day the fund order is made` `to` `the day I claimed`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day the fund order is made` `to` `today`

-- s 88: "A judgment given in representative proceedings binds all group members affected by it, other than any person who
-- has opted out of the proceedings under section 71." "other than": JUST FALSE for a person who opted out. A group member
-- the judgment does not affect (s 86(5): the judgment is to "describe or otherwise identify the group members who will be
-- affected by it"): the section is silent, NOTHING.
GIVEN `I opted out under s 71` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment describes or identifies me as affected by it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 -- the judgment binds me` `I opted out under s 71` `the judgment describes or identifies me as affected by it` MEANS
    IF `I opted out under s 71` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the judgment describes or identifies me as affected by it` THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 88 binds group members affected by the judgment and says nothing of others)

§§ `Division 5 -- appeals (s 89(3))`

-- s 89(3): "If the representative party or the sub-group representative party does not institute an appeal within the time
-- allowed for doing so, another member of the group or sub-group may, within a further 21-day period, institute an appeal as
-- representing the group members or sub-group members." The time allowed is set elsewhere (s 40 and the Rules of Court, not
-- encoded): its last day is an input. The further period runs from the day after that last day for 21 days (fork F12).
--
-- Two-step regulative rule, day 0 the day of the judgment: the representative party DOes appeal WITHIN the time allowed,
-- HENCE FULFILLED (no s 89(3) appeal arises); LEST, from the day after that last day, the other member DOes appeal WITHIN
-- 20 more days (21 days counting the first), LEST BREACH. The trace starts the second rule with a WAITUNTIL on the day
-- after the first deadline.
DECLARE `Appeal party` IS ONE OF `the representative party`, `another group member`
DECLARE `Appeal act` IS ONE OF `institute an appeal for the group`

GIVEN `the last day for the representative party` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 89(3) -- the last day of the further 21-day period` `the last day for the representative party` MEANS `the date` 21 `days after` `the last day for the representative party`

GIVEN `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the representative party` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Appeal party` `Appeal act`
`s 89(3) -- the group's appeal` `the day of the judgment` `the last day for the representative party` MEANS
    PARTY `the representative party`
    DO `institute an appeal for the group`
    WITHIN (`the days from` `the day of the judgment` `to` `the last day for the representative party`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `another group member`
        DO `institute an appeal for the group`
        WITHIN 20
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `another group member` BECAUSE "no appeal by the representative party in the time allowed, nor by another member within the further 21 days (s 89(3))"

DECLARE `Where my appeal for the group stands` IS ONE OF
    `s 89(3) does not arise: the representative party appealed in time`
    `not yet: the representative party's own time has not run out`
    `in time: within the further 21 days (s 89(3))`
    `still open: I can appeal for the group within the further 21 days (s 89(3))`
    `out of time under s 89(3)`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Appeal party` `Appeal act`
      `the start of the further period` IS A NUMBER
      `the time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a member's appeal is in time under` `the rule` `from` `the start of the further period` `at` `the time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the start of the further period`), (EVENT `another group member` `institute an appeal for the group` `the time`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the representative party` IS A DATE
      `the representative party appealed in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have appealed for the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I appealed` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where my appeal for the group stands`
`s 89(3) -- where my appeal for the group stands` `the day of the judgment` `the last day for the representative party` `the representative party appealed in time` `I have appealed for the group` `the day I appealed` `today` MEANS
    IF `the representative party appealed in time`
    THEN `s 89(3) does not arise: the representative party appealed in time`
    ELSE IF `the time` AT MOST `the last time`
         THEN `not yet: the representative party's own time has not run out`
         ELSE IF `a member's appeal is in time under` (`s 89(3) -- the group's appeal` `the day of the judgment` `the last day for the representative party`) `from` (`the last time` PLUS 1) `at` `the time`
              THEN IF `I have appealed for the group` THEN `in time: within the further 21 days (s 89(3))` ELSE `still open: I can appeal for the group within the further 21 days (s 89(3))`
              ELSE `out of time under s 89(3)`
    WHERE
        `the last time` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the judgment` `to` `the last day for the representative party`
        `the time` MEANS
            IF `I have appealed for the group`
            THEN `the days from` `the day of the judgment` `to` `the day I appealed`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day of the judgment` `to` `today`

§§ `Division 6 -- limitation periods (s 89B)`

DECLARE `What has happened to the class action` IS ONE OF
    `it is still running`
    `I opted out under s 71`
    `the proceeding was discontinued`
    `the proceeding and any appeals were determined without finally disposing of my claim`
    `the proceeding and any appeals finally disposed of my claim`
    `the Court ordered that it no longer continue as a class action (ss 73-76)`

DECLARE `My limitation period` IS ONE OF
    `Part VII does not govern this proceeding`
    `not suspended: my claim was already out of time when the class action began (s 89B(3))`
    `suspended while the class action runs (s 89B(1))`
    `running again (s 89B(2))`
    `no longer matters: my claim has been finally disposed of`
    `the Act does not say: an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action is not one of the s 89B(2) events`

-- s 89B(1): "On the commencement of any representative proceedings, the running of the limitation period that applies to the
-- claim of a group member to which the proceedings relate is suspended." (2): "The limitation period does not begin to run
-- again unless - (a) the member opts out of the proceedings under section 71; or (b) the proceedings are discontinued; or
-- (c) the proceedings, and any appeals arising from the proceedings, are determined without finally disposing of the group
-- member's claim." (3): "nothing in this section affects the running of a limitation period in respect of a group member
-- who, immediately before the commencement of the representative proceedings, was barred by the expiration of that period".
-- (4): "despite anything in the Limitation Act 1974". The limitation period itself is set elsewhere (the Limitation Act
-- 1974, not encoded): its last day is an input. A claim whose last day is before the day the class action was commenced
-- was barred; one whose last day is that day was not (fork F13).
GIVEN `Part VII applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day the class action was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action` IS A DATE
      `what has happened` IS A `What has happened to the class action`
GIVETH A `My limitation period`
`s 89B -- my limitation period` `Part VII applies` `the day the class action was commenced` `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action` `what has happened` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part VII applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN `Part VII does not govern this proceeding`
    ELSE IF `the days from` `the day the class action was commenced` `to` `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action` LESS THAN 0
         THEN `not suspended: my claim was already out of time when the class action began (s 89B(3))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `what has happened`
              WHEN `it is still running` THEN `suspended while the class action runs (s 89B(1))`
              WHEN `I opted out under s 71` THEN `running again (s 89B(2))`
              WHEN `the proceeding was discontinued` THEN `running again (s 89B(2))`
              WHEN `the proceeding and any appeals were determined without finally disposing of my claim` THEN `running again (s 89B(2))`
              WHEN `the proceeding and any appeals finally disposed of my claim` THEN `no longer matters: my claim has been finally disposed of`
              WHEN `the Court ordered that it no longer continue as a class action (ss 73-76)` THEN `the Act does not say: an order that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action is not one of the s 89B(2) events`

-- The new last day once the period runs again. "Suspended" is read as stopping the clock: the days left on the day the
-- class action was commenced (that day still counting as one on which the member could sue) are added to the day the
-- period begins to run again (fork F13). The day it runs again: the day the opt-out notice was given, the day of
-- discontinuance, or the day of the final determination (fork F14). Where the claim was already barred, s 89B changes
-- nothing: the original last day. Where the period is still suspended, or the Act does not say, NOTHING.
GIVEN `Part VII applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day the class action was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action` IS A DATE
      `what has happened` IS A `What has happened to the class action`
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 89B -- the last day to start my own proceeding` `Part VII applies` `the day the class action was commenced` `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action` `what has happened` `the day it happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 89B -- my limitation period` `Part VII applies` `the day the class action was commenced` `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action` `what has happened`
    WHEN `not suspended: my claim was already out of time when the class action began (s 89B(3))` THEN JUST `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action`
    WHEN `running again (s 89B(2))` THEN JUST (`the date` (`the days from` `the day the class action was commenced` `to` `the last day of my limitation period, apart from the class action`) `days after` `the day it happened`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: suspended with no end yet, Part VII not governing, a claim finally disposed of, or an event s 89B(2) does not list)

§§ `Division 6 -- reimbursement of the representative party's costs (s 89D)`

-- s 89D(1): "If the Court has made an award of damages in representative proceedings, the representative party or a
-- sub-group representative party, or a person who has been such a party, may apply". (2): "If ... the Court is satisfied
-- that the costs reasonably incurred in relation to the representative proceedings by the applicant are likely to exceed the
-- costs recoverable by the applicant from the defendant, the Court may order that an amount equal to the whole or a part of
-- the excess be paid to the applicant out of the damages awarded." No award of damages, or the Court not satisfied: "if"
-- fails, JUST FALSE. A person who never was a representative party: outside (1)'s list, NOTHING.
GIVEN `I am or have been the representative party or a sub-group representative party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has made an award of damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied my reasonable costs are likely to exceed the costs I can recover from the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89D -- the Court may order the excess of my costs paid out of the damages` `I am or have been the representative party or a sub-group representative party` `the Court has made an award of damages` `the Court is satisfied my reasonable costs are likely to exceed the costs I can recover from the defendant` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am or have been the representative party or a sub-group representative party`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 89D(1) lists who may apply)
    ELSE IF `the Court has made an award of damages` AND `the Court is satisfied my reasonable costs are likely to exceed the costs I can recover from the defendant`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
